🐢 paddle out — swap to kai@x.com
🐢 heads up — swapped in kai@x.com, but could not stow moana@x.com into the keyrack
   its ONLY token is now <tmp>/.credentials.json.bak. rescue it:
     1. cp <tmp>/.credentials.json.bak <tmp>/.credentials.json
     2. brains.auth.set          # files moana@x.com back into the keyrack
     3. rm -f <tmp>/.credentials.json.bak
     4. brains.auth.use --reach kai@x.com   # swap back to where you meant to be
   ⚠️ that file holds a live token in the clear; it is kept ONLY because the keyrack
      copy failed. until it is rescued, every swap REFUSES rather than overwrite it.
   └─ signed in as kai@x.com 🧠

🐢 heads up — claude sessions already open still hold the old token; restart them
